  "limitations": [
    "The corpus is generated, not harvested from the field: it is a controlled damage matrix, not a sample of how archives break in the wild. Nothing here estimates real-world recovery rates.",
    "Only ZIP is covered. No conclusion about RAR, 7z or any other container follows from it.",
    "Every archive is stored/DEFLATE, unencrypted and non-ZIP64. Cases where VERAQIS abstains by design (encryption, ZIP64, unsupported methods) are therefore not represented, and its recovery rate here is not a rate over all real archives.",
    "One host, one OS, one filesystem. Timing and memory figures do not transfer to other hardware.",
    "At least one tool provides no machine-readable entry listing, so entry-discovery rate is not comparable across all tools; it is reported as *not measured* for those.",
    "At least one tool cannot attribute errors to individual files, so its flag-aware false-recovery figure cannot be computed; cross-tool comparison must use the strict column.",
    "No Android application was measured in this run. No statement about Android archivers may be derived from it."
  ],
